  "context_pill": "PGBP Computation & Statutory Deductions",
  "example_summary": "Isac Limited, a biotechnology firm, must adjust its net profit by filtering out disallowed capital expenditures (like land for R&D and skill development) and non-business items (like political ads and tax loan interest) to compute its taxable PGBP income for AY 2026-27.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix: Corporate PGBP Adjustments\n\n| Area / Head | Statutory Section / Rule | Operative Threshold / Condition | Tax Treatment / Legal Consequence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| In-House Research | Section 35(1)(iv) & 35(2) | Capital expenditure on scientific research | Land cost disallowed; Building cost 100% allowed |\n| Biotech Research | Section 35(2AB) | Raw material and revenue expenditure for approved R&D | Qualifies for 100% deduction |\n| Agricultural Extension | Section 35CCC | Expenditure on notified agricultural extension project | 100% deduction allowed |\n| Skill Development | Section 35CCD | Expenditure on notified skill development project | Land cost disallowed; Training expenses 100% allowed |\n| Political Advertisements | Section 37(2B) | Advertisement in souvenir published by political party | Strictly disallowed as PGBP expense |\n\n\n> [!NOTE] Capital vs Revenue Disallowances: Expenses of a capital nature such as issue of right shares are disallowed under PGBP, whereas debenture issue expenses are allowed as revenue expenditure.\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Non-Business and Penalty Disallowances: Interest on loan taken for advance tax payment and penalties for violating civil/criminal laws (like GST penalties) are inadmissible, whereas contractual breach damages are allowable business losses.",
